Day 1 – Git Basics & Repository Setup

What I did:
- Created a local directory to practice Git commands

- Initialized a Git repository using git init

- Created a simple Bash script (calculator.sh) to understand file tracking

- Learned the Git workflow:
  . git status
  . git add
  . git commit

- Understood the difference between:
  . A local-only Git repository
  . A remote GitHub repository

- Created a public GitHub repository (deployment-basics)

- Cloned the GitHub repository to my local machine

- Copied the Bash script into the cloned repository

- Committed the file inside the cloned repo

- Learned why GitHub no longer allows password-based authentication

- Set up SSH authentication for GitHub

- Switched the repository remote from HTTPS to SSH

- Successfully pushed the code to GitHub using git push
